  "details": "Now that we have wrist buttons for the QM, I would love to see this system extended to replace all the annoying pinch gestures. It's way too easy to accidentally hit several pinch gestures while gesticulating with your hands, and toggling the lock is slow and cumbersome. The entire point of having hand tracking is to articulate with your hands, and its s shame I have to keep my hands idle most of the time for fear of hitting random pinch gestures and being set running across the room. \n\nI would much prefer if all the current pinch gestures were replaced with floating buttons. Even the movement controls could be replaced by a floating physical joystick(s) that you can grab and pull around. \n\nIt's important to remember that the Quest hand tracking system is specifically trained only on thumb and index finger pinch with the palm facing away from your body. All the other pinches are difficult for it to determine, and the accuracy only gets lower each finger further from the index. On a Quest 2/Pro pinky pinches are almost impossible to execute.",
